{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T13:36:06.218Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 complete. Summary:\n\n**Changed (in scope only):**\n- `src/core/linter.ts` — added local OpenSpec validator integration: resolves `node_modules/.bin/openspec`, reads the resolved version from `node_modules/@fission-ai/openspec/package.json`, runs both `validate --changes` and `validate --specs` with `--strict --json --no-interactive` under `OPENSPEC_TELEMETRY=0`, parses JSON findings with the `openspec:` prefix, logs/warns once on a version mismatch vs `1.13.1`, and verifies delta targets against base specs via `mergeDelta`.\n- `src/cli/lint.ts` (new) — `lintCommand` with optional IDs, injectable exit sink, non-zero exit on failure.\n- `src/cli/index.ts` — registered `lint [ids...]`.\n- `tests/linter.test.ts` — 11 new tests alongside the 8 legacy ones.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/linter.test.ts` → 19/19 pass.\n- `pnpm verify` (tsc + 378 tests + biome) → all green.\n\n**Notable context:** Task 1's declared changes (`paths.openspecRoot`, `config.openspec`, `@fission-ai/openspec` pin) are absent from the working tree despite being marked `[x]`, so I accessed those settings defensively as task 3 already did, and documented this in the result file. The real `openspec validate --json` schema couldn't be inspected (package not installed), so the parser is intentionally tolerant.\n\nResult written to `specs/016-openspec-artifacts/.run/results/4.md`."}}
